#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:0
msgid ""
"Complete reference for requesting and reviewing snap aliases, interface auto-"
"connections, and tracks through the Snap Store process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:8
msgid "Process for aliases, auto-connections and tracks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:10
msgid "Definitions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:12
msgid ""
"Reviewers are in the [@reviewers](https://forum.snapcraft.io/groups/"
"reviewers) private forum group (access restricted)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:13
msgid "Architects are those responsible for the design of snapd."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:14
msgid "Votes are in favor (+1), against (-1), abstain (+0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:15
msgid "Voting period is one week"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:16
msgid "Voting period extension is 3 days"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:18
msgid "Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:20
msgid ""
"Requester creates a forum post in [the relevant store-requests subcategory]"
"(https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/about-the-store-requests-category/10871), "
"using the subcategory template to provide all the required details . Voting "
"period starts at time of request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:21
msgid "Requester may not vote on his/her own snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:22
msgid ""
"Reviewers and/or architects vote using the voting procedure (see below). "
"Each vote should include a short rationale for the cast vote (longer "
"rationale is required for voting contrary to an established pattern)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:23
msgid ""
"If after voting period there are not enough votes based on voting procedure, "
"a voting period extension should be requested by a reviewer/architect. The "
"extension starts the day of the request for extension"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:24
msgid ""
"At the end of the voting period, a reviewer/architects tallies the results "
"from the voting period (and extension), summarizes in the forum post and "
"performs any necessary actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:26
msgid "Voting procedure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:28
msgid ""
"The voting procedure is the same for granting and revoking auto-connections, "
"auto-aliases and track requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:29
msgid ""
"If reviewers and up to at most one architect voted: simple majority with at "
"least 2 votes in favor at end of voting period/extension: perform requested "
"action. In the event of a tie, request more votes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:30
msgid ""
"If two or more votes in favor/against from architects: reviewers votes are "
"not tallied. If have only in favor votes from architects at end of voting "
"period/extension: perform requested action, otherwise architects discuss "
"until no against votes and at least one vote in favor from architects. If "
"clear direction from architects, an architect may request the vote be "
"tallied early."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:32
msgid "alias request considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:33
msgid ""
"Granting aliases requires trust in the snap's publisher and reasonable names "
"for the aliases (eg, shouldn't request an alias for something that is a "
"widely known command of other software)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:35
msgid ""
"An alias should not be granted for the snap's name since snapd already "
"grants use of this name to the snap (eg, a snap named 'foo' with command "
"'foo.foo2' should not be granted the 'foo' alias, instead, the snap can "
"rename the 'foo2' command to be 'foo' instead (and optionally request an "
"alias for the 'foo2' command))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:37
msgid "auto-connection request considerations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:39
msgid ""
"In the snap ecosystem it is important to remember that there are several "
"voices when considering auto-connection: snapd (base declaration policy), "
"the gadget snap (for device-specific auto-connections, which does not apply "
"to auto-connection requests), the store (snap declaration policy; ie, "
"requests using this process) and the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:41
msgid ""
"For each snap interface, a determination is made for whether or not the "
"interface should be manual or automatically connected based on a variety of "
"criteria (the rationale is often in the snapd code base or pull requests) "
"and this is codified in the base declaration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:43
msgid ""
"A snap's publisher may request that a normally manually-connected interface "
"be auto-connected for a particular snap in the global, public store using "
"the process outlined in this topic (brand store owners may grant auto-"
"connections as appropriate for their brand). Granting auto-connection in the "
"global, public store effectually means that the store is vouching for the "
"publisher's intent (maintenance, security updates, etc) and snap "
"implementation (it does what it advertises, works well, etc) to the degree "
"that the user's initial choice on connection at install time is removed (the "
"user may of course disconnect the interface after installation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:45
msgid ""
"Reviewers must therefore consider various criteria to inform their vote on "
"whether the request will be granted. Some of this criteria might include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:47
msgid "The \"officialness\" of the publisher of the snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:48
msgid ""
"The \"reasonableness\" of the request. Eg, a \"top-like\" program will "
"necessarily need the \"system-observe\" interface but not \"network-control\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:49
msgid ""
"The snap name makes it clear that an interface should be auto-connected. Eg, "
"a snap named \"webcam\" with it declaring the \"camera\" interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:50
msgid "The software is intended to be used by children"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:51
msgid ""
"The sensitivity of the access relative to the \"user's voice\" (see above)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:53
msgid ""
"For some interfaces there are patterns and rationale that can generally be "
"applied. Please note the rationale is subject to change based on security "
"concerns from the community (users, publishers, reviewers, snapd developers, "
"etc), more appropriate technologies becoming available, new information and/"
"or critical thinking, etc. Each request will be reviewed on its own merits "
"and prior granting of auto-connection may be rescinded based on this new "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:55
msgid ""
"alsa - auto-connection is generally limited to snaps requiring low-level, "
"direct access to audio devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:56
msgid ""
"Rationale: a lot of hardware does not perform multiplexing of clients so a "
"snap directly accessing the hardware might block audio for other "
"applications on some systems. Sound servers like pulseaudio are designed to "
"multiplex audio and snaps should typically instead plugs the `audio-"
"playback` (and `audio-record` if needed), which grants access to pulseaudio"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:57
msgid "Reference: {ref}`alsa interface <interfaces-alsa-interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:58
msgid ""
"content - the base declaration defines that snaps that plugs the content "
"interface will auto-connect with other snaps from the same publisher. Global "
"auto-connect for content providers is allowed only under certain "
"circumstances"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:59
msgid ""
"Rationale: because there is no tight coupling or dependency graphs between "
"the provider and the consumer, there are no guarantees that a providing snap "
"cannot break consuming snaps. Publishers are expected to manage breaking "
"changes with their snaps, but are not generally expected to be concerned "
"about others' snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:60
#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:68
#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:73
msgid "Reference:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:61
msgid ""
"https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/auto-connection-for-gnome-3-24-content-"
"interface/1379/51"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:62
msgid ""
"https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/allow-global-autoconnect-kde-frameworks-5-"
"qt-5-14-core18/16335/4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:63
msgid ""
"content for theme snaps - in addition to the above considerations, "
"eventually snapd might suggest or auto-install theme snaps based on various "
"criteria. Until review-tools checks are fully in place, if a publisher "
"requests global auto-connection with greedy plugs, reviewers should:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:64
msgid ""
"ensure the snap only slots the agreed to content identifiers (ie, `content` "
"attribute or interface reference if `content` attribute is omitted)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:65
msgid ""
"ensure the snap ships only (valid) content files (eg, css, images, audio "
"files, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:66
msgid "ensure the theme snap does not ship any commands, daemon or hooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:67
msgid ""
"vet the publisher (part of vetting shall include an agreement to agree to "
"adhering to the above going forward)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:69
msgid ""
"https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/auto-connect-custom-gtk-themes-to-gtk-3-themes-"
"gtk-2-themes-and-icon-themes/17354/3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:70
msgid ""
"https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/auto-connect-and-greedy-plug-behaviour-for-for-"
"gtk-common-themes-and-gtk-theme-traditionalhumanized-snaps/19113/6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:71
msgid ""
"cups-control - auto-connection is limited to snaps whose core functionality "
"is printing or design programs where printing is an expected part of the "
"workflow. Granting requires a stated commitment from the developer that "
"moving to a safer API will be performed (such as the Printing portal) when "
"it is widely available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:72
msgid ""
"Rationale: cups-control unfortunately grants access to the CUPS socket which "
"on a typical single user system, grants admin privileges for printer "
"configuration, which is more than the intended permission to allow printing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:74
msgid ""
"https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/inkscape-autoconnect-cups-control/8739/39 "
"(initial)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:75
msgid ""
"https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/inkscape-autoconnect-cups-control/8739/40 "
"(revisited)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:76
msgid "joystick - auto-connection generally limited to game snaps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:77
msgid ""
"mpris - slot side is generally granted provided the `name` attribute makes "
"sense for the snap. auto-connection of plugs is typically not auto-connected "
"[unless the slot's publisher also agrees](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/auto-"
"connect-request-for-lyricfier/15533/18)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:78
msgid ""
"password-manager-service - typically not auto-connected due to the sensitive "
"nature of the access and because the user's voice in this access is so "
"important"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:79
msgid ""
"Rationale: the various keyring services do not provide sufficient isolation "
"for snap access to the interface to be auto-connected by default. Not only "
"can the snap see all stored passwords, but all other applications with "
"access to the password services can also see the snap's passwords."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:80
msgid ""
"Reference: https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/nordpass-auto-connect-to-password-"
"manager-service-interface/14968/5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:81
msgid ""
"removable-media: typically not auto-connected since the optional access to "
"widely varied data does not outweigh the user's voice regarding potentially "
"sensitive data. Certain classes of applications may be granted an exception "
"under certain circumstances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:82
msgid ""
"Rationale: by definition data that is not always present (as is the case "
"with removable-media) is optional access for typical snaps. All snaps with "
"this interface connected have unrestricted access to all data from any "
"plugged media. Considering that removable-media may contain sensitive "
"documents, sensitive pictures/media, encryption keys, etc and that snapd has "
"no insight on the nature of the data, the user's voice with regard to "
"connection is preserved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:83
msgid ""
"Exceptions: the following classes of applications may be considered for "
"removable-media auto-connection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:84
msgid ""
"major browsers and email clients (rationale: the software is designed with "
"security and user privacy in mind)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:85
msgid ""
"media (eg, sound, photo, video) editors (rationale: the software is very "
"often used to import/edit/export large files on external devices)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:86
msgid ""
"media (eg, sound, photo, video) players/viewers (rationale: the software is "
"very often used to import/preview/playback files on external devices)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:87
msgid ""
"media (eg, sound, photo, video) recorders/cameras (rationale: the software "
"is very often used to export/edit files on external devices)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:89
msgid ""
"If the application falls into one of the above categories, then the "
"following criteria will also be considered:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:90
msgid "the application itself is a mature, well-known application"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:91
msgid "the snap's (vetted) publisher is a mature, well-known entity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:92
msgid "the snap's (vetted) publisher is the upstream of the software"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:93
msgid ""
"if the snap is published by someone other than upstream, the publisher must "
"be vetted and either be an established committer to the upstream or the "
"wider snap ecosystem (eg, an established well-known contributor to the "
"software itself, a member of the snapcrafters group, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:94
msgid ""
"if the publisher doesn't meet these criteria, other options may or may not "
"be considered such as the publisher joining snapcrafters, snapcrafters "
"becoming a collaborator on the snap, auto-connection granted conditional on "
"the snap packaging being accepted upstream, upstream stating they trust the "
"publisher with the packaging, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:95
msgid "Additional information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:96
msgid ""
"The removable-media interface is considered a 'transitional' interface "
"since, when connected, only traditional UNIX permissions are considered for "
"file access. This allows, for example, a service in a snap to setup inotify/"
"etc to programmatically monitor and exfiltrate/modify files on external "
"media in the background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:97
msgid ""
"Eventually, applications will either use safer APIs for file access (eg, "
"like portals) or future snapd-prompting mechanisms may be available to "
"obviate the need for auto-connecting this interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:98
msgid ""
"Security-conscious users may want to remove sensitive external media when "
"installing snaps, then disconnect the interface from those snaps to prevent "
"them from having access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:99
msgid ""
"In the future, snapd may grow controls to disable certain interface auto-"
"connections for interfaces like removable-media"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:100
msgid ""
"uinput: typically not auto-connected because it allows injecting arbitrary "
"input into the system. In addition, due to popular hardware/software "
"instructions outside of the snap ecosystem, `/dev/uinput` may be world read "
"and writable (default udev rules create it as root-owned with only root read "
"and writable). Due to these considerations, publishers requesting use of "
"(and especially auto-connect) should be vetted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:102
msgid "Manual connection mitigations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:104
msgid "If auto-connection is not granted, options for snap publishers are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:105
msgid ""
"have the snap check if the interface is connected via `snapctl is-connected "
"<iface>` and instruct the user to use the `snap connect` CLI command or "
"connect via the snap-store/gnome-software GUI. This could be done on startup "
"or contextually at the time of access. Ideally when instructing the user, "
"the details of the access would be explained so the user can make an "
"informed choice. It is true that there is an extra step for the user, but "
"done well, this need not be onerous and may even provide additional trust "
"that your snap and the system as a whole are working to keep everything "
"secure. Note, if using `snapctl is-connected` you should also add a "
"corresponding `assumes: 2.43` to your snapcraft.yaml since this is only "
"available in snap since 2.43 to ensure this [functions as expected](https://"
"forum.snapcraft.io/t/interfaces-for-raspberry-pi-imager/15822/20)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:106
msgid ""
"use a newer, safer API. Eg, instead of using cups-control, the application "
"could use [the Printing portal](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/inkscape-"
"autoconnect-cups-control/8739/52). If an application needs access to a file "
"from a disconnected interface/etc, use a file dialog that supports {ref}"
"`portals <interfaces-xdg-desktop-portals>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:107
msgid ""
"fallback gracefully. Eg, if password-manager-service is disconnected, "
"fallback to storing passwords locally"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:109
msgid ""
"In the future, the snapd team plans to provide a [prompt API for snaps to "
"use ](https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/inkscape-autoconnect-cups-control/"
"8739/39) that will not only provide appropriate messaging, but also allow "
"the user to choose to connect within the prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:111
msgid ""
"Finally, the desktop team has discussed the lack of isolation in secret-"
"service with upstream GNOME and there are plans to [improve the service]"
"(https://wiki.gnome.org/Projects/GnomeKeyring/SecurityPhilosophy) (see "
"'Active Attacks') to provide the necessary isolation for auto-connecting. "
"Hopefully, KDE/Plasma will follow with kwallet or move to the improved "
"service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:113
msgid "Tracks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/administration/process-for-aliases-auto-connections-and-tracks.md:115
msgid ""
"There is a [simplified process for tracks for snaps with predictable cadence]"
"(https://forum.snapcraft.io/t/simplified-track-request-process-for-snaps-"
"with-predictable-cadence/3136)."
msgstr ""
